Package: svysem
Title: Design-Based Structural Equation Models for Complex Surveys
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: person("Siyang", "Ni", email = "johnni.nj@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Design-based estimation of structural equation models uses a model
    for 'lavaan' and a design from 'survey' as input, including a subpopulation
    taken with subset(). Sampling weights, strata, and primary sampling units
    enter the variance the way 'Mplus' does with TYPE=COMPLEX (Oberski (2014)
    <doi:10.18637/jss.v057.i01>). The design-based covariance of the sample
    moments goes to 'lavaan' with the raw data and the weights. svysem(),
    svycfa(), and svygrowth() are the three fitters. svysem() fits a structural
    equation model, svycfa() a confirmatory factor analysis, and svygrowth() a
    growth curve. The result extends the 'lavaan' fit, so coef(), vcov(), and
    fitMeasures() are design-based. Each completed data set of a multiple
    imputation is fitted on its own and pooled with Rubin's rules (Rubin (1987)
    <doi:10.1002/9780470316696>). pooled_estimates() and pooled_wald() use the
    survey design's degrees of freedom as the complete-data degrees of freedom
    (Barnard and Rubin (1999) <doi:10.1093/biomet/86.4.948>). fitMeasures()
    reports a pooled scaled chi-square and the mean, minimum, and maximum of the
    robust fit indices. Those indices are not pooled with Rubin's rules. This
    version fits complete continuous data with maximum likelihood and a
    Satorra-Bentler adjustment. Ordinal weighted least squares, robust maximum
    likelihood, factor scores, and replicate-weight designs are not in this
    version.
